  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was a mixed signal. Port Washington delivered strong growth\u2014grooming revenue up 20% and total revenue up 15%\u2014but that strength is isolated to one day. Month-to-date, Port Washington remains flat while Hicksville is accelerating, up 21% for April. Year-to-date you're crushing it: 53% revenue growth and 55% more appointments across both locations. That's real progress.\n\nHere's what needs attention. Retail is broken at both stores. Port Washington retail dropped 9%, Hicksville cratered 62%. Your bully stick inventory is completely depleted at Port Washington while Hicksville is hemorrhaging X-Small Treat Table stock (43 units monthly, now 287 units in the hole). This isn't a supply chain delay\u2014this is demand you're not capturing. Restock these items immediately; they're your margin drivers.\n\nStore supplies are tighter than they should be. Port Washington needs ear cleaner, brown bags, Quick Dry, and Windex now. Hicksville has five items out and seven more at critical reorder level. This creates operational friction that will slow your groomers down.\n\nHicksville's grooming business is heating up\u201431% growth yesterday, 23% appointment growth month-to-date. That's your growth engine. Protect that momentum by solving the inventory problem this week."
